  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-28 at dev 5f80a79081. PREMISE HOLDS. THE TAINT ARM, left UNMEASURED at filing, is now measured and IS A FALSE ALL-CLEAR. Record: scratchpad satal/run.py. Claim: taint_flow host_secret -> prohibited_sink_zone subprocess, built-in labels.\n\nSHIPPED verify-claims, one file each; the only difference is how the sink is reached:\n  python  direct: os.environ -> subprocess.run in go()           violated (ddg, confirmed walk)\n  python  via a function: go() -> launch(cmd) -> subprocess.run  violated (ddg_mixed)\n  python  via a constructor: go() -> Runner(cmd) -> __init__ -> subprocess.run\n          CONFIRMED_WITH_CAVEATS, 0 evidence. The only caveat is opaque_boundary about the subprocess.run launch, which says nothing about the missed flow.\n  js      via a function                                          violated\n  js      via a constructor (new Runner(cmd), execSync in constructor)   CONFIRMED_WITH_CAVEATS\n  java    via a constructor                                       inconclusive, for an unrelated reason (method-shaped catalogue gate). The edge shape is the same.\nEdge shape as the row says: 'instantiates go -> Runner:class' (python, js), 'App.go -> App.Runner:class' (java). No edge reaches __init__ / constructor.\n\nWHAT IS NOT LOST: a boundary claim (must_not_exist subprocess). The sink call inside __init__ is its own edge, so the chain is still reported and the claim is violated. The loss is REACHABILITY THROUGH the construction: taint flows here, and per the row io_boundary's traced paths and slice. Only the taint arm was run today.\n\nDirection note stands and matters for the fix: this arm ADDS findings (recall). The dead-code fix removed false ones.\nNOT DONE: sizing on a corpus (how many flows a construction hop would add). The row asks for that before choosing (a) the shared helper over cli._construction_initializer_edges (still at cli.py:8251) or (b) re-pointing the dst."  # 413e
