  message: "DONE in PR #1274 (merged; fix commit cc34ba323c). New core module construction.py holds the construction rule every walk reads. initializer_hops (class -> initializer, moved out of cli.py, still importable there under its old name for the dead-code tests) and construction_calls (caller -> initializer, line). taint gets caller->initializer call edges in memory (cli verify-claims, per language); io_boundary adds them to its reverse graph; slice follows the one contains edge a construction licenses, in both directions. No emitted edge changes (the reasons option (b) was priced out still hold).\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, the row's repros re-run on merged dev (scratchpad satal/):\n  taint host_secret -> subprocess through a constructor: python confirmed_with_caveats/0 -> VIOLATED/1 (ddg_mixed, as the through-a-function control); javascript (new Runner(cmd), execSync in constructor) same -> VIOLATED.\n  io-boundaries: subprocess.run in Runner.__init__ entry_points [] -> [main].\n  slice --entry main: now contains Runner.__init__ and subprocess.run; reverse slice from Runner.__init__ finds main and go (test).\nTests: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_construction_reaches_initializer_everywhere.py (6), plus the existing dead-code suite unchanged.\n\nSIZE, as this row demanded, record ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/satal_09282026/RESULT.md:\n  TAINT: ZERO measured effect on the corpus sample. kserve 34 flows, feast 11, prospector 0, IDENTICAL sets A vs B across 5 built-in flow claims. The fixture-level false all-clear is fixed; no corpus instance was found in these three repos. Not dressed as recall.\n  IO REACH (feast): 32 chains gained entry points (chains with >=1 EP 452 -> 476), e.g. sqlite3.connect in _initialize_conn 0 -> 49, os.getenv in KubernetesMaterializer.__init__ 0 -> 1.\n  SLICE: fixtures only; not measured on a corpus.\nNOT CHANGED: the ruby / csharp / java constructor shapes, which already land on a callable."  # 6a18
